Z||000000||Songman||09-02-2001||01:37 AM||||Apparently at least one person here thinks so since I don't agree with him... Don't you, LZeitgeist?<P>Personally, I say you may or may not agree with me but I am consistent in my views.. and that is for a person's rights...<P>He bases his idea that I am a hypocrite on this thread... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003191.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003191.html</A>  LZeitgeist <BR>Even after I pointed out that he missed key words or phrases in what I said, he then had to quote it... AND STILL MISSED THE POINT.. but at least he did it with a lot of very flambouyant name calling. And I'm still so upset that he lost respest for me...<P>So anyway... I am opening myself up to all of your shots. Fire away! Am I a hypocrite?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Urchin||09-02-2001||02:10 AM||||Sorry to see that that thread turned ugly.  I had stopped following it. Whether you are a hypocrite or not... ?  I have never read any posts of yours in the past that I would label as hipocracy.  When it comes to this particular thread, I guess I would have to hear your bike    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If it is excessively loud, then perhaps he has a point.  But if what you are claiming holds true ("sounds good but not as loud as these stereos" I believe is how you put it) then I would say no, you are not being hypocritical.   That is my opinion, probably not much help.  <BR>On a side note, a neighbour of mine has a harley (loudest thing I have ever heard).  He seems to be cruising at all hours of the night.  My roommate and I have to shout to hear each other as he passes by.  This is excessively loud.  Unacceptable.  But as someone stated in that thread(not sure who), it's o.k. for bikes to be that loud but not cars.  The safety factor is true to a point, but only to a point.  I don't think there is a risk of being hit by a car 4 blocks away, so why is it necessary for them to hear you that far away?   Good luck resolving your dispute.<BR>I can't say I have ever known anyone interested in both harleys and fieros... interesting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">    <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<P>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-02-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||1
