Z||000008||rogergarrison||09-02-2001||08:25 AM||||I dont think so. If you follow most of the posts in the thread, youll see most people agree that you shouldnt force everyone to listen to your music. Was no need to get into a name calling match. I dont agree with songman lots of times, but we usually treat each other civily. That respect for other people and there view too. I bet you were the kid that if you wernt allowed to be captain, you took your ball home. If you wanna hear your car radio loud go out driving in the country and enjoy yourself to your hearts content.||||reg||1
Z||000009||LZeitgeist||09-02-2001||08:53 AM||||Quoted from Songman in thread [link]http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003191.html[/link]<P>(all quotes listed are Songman's own words, unless otherwise stated)<BR>      <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I've posted here several times what I think about this... <P>I shouldn't have to listen to someone else's music at a redlight... hearing their music over my own! And I certainly shouldn't have to hear it in my house at night over my television... If it weren't so pathetic I would laugh at people that do that.. hear all the nut vibrating loose in their cars... and no, it doesn't matter if it is rock, rap, or anything else... be a little bit courteous to the people around you.. That is the bottom line. It seems that society has forgotten all about that.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>      <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>And I have to admit to one of the first things I did after I got my Harley was to get rid of the stock exhaust and put some slant tips on it... Sounds good.. but still not as lound as these stereos... even when I get into it!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>      <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>You're exactly right! And that is why bikes have to be loud! It is a lot harder to see a guy on a bike than it is a big ole car. Not that most people care because they'll cut you off no matter what.. then flip you off when you get pissed like it was your fault... people are idiots...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>      <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I pointed out over and over that my Harley wasn't loud!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>      <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Here is a tip for anyone that falls into that category... You are not cool. You are annoying. Hit the interstate and let it fly! Rattle your car apart if you want, but respect us when we are in earshot of you. People will think you are much cooler if they can also think you are a human being that knows how to be courteous to other people. And besides all of this stuff... if I can hear the music five cars away and all I can hear is your car rattling and the bass... how can it possibly sound good inside your car? The truth is that it can't! You are doing it to try to make people think you are cool... I am in the music business. I understand sound. There is no way it sounds good to you...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Um... yeah. He runs open pipes on a Harley to be heard and seen, "but they're not loud!"     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> (if it's not loud, then how can you be 'seen'?), and yet complains about stereo-pumpers (which I don't care for either) being discourteous to other people.  Also, not surprisingly, when I paraphrased one of his complaints about stereo sounds to reflect exhaust sounds (all caps reflect the altered words - nothing else has been changed in any way) (quoted from me here)<BR>     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Let's paraphrase something, shall we?<P>"I shouldn't have to listen to someone else's EXHAUST at a redlight... hearing their EXHAUST over my own! And I certainly shouldn't have to hear it in my house at night over my television... If it weren't so pathetic I would laugh at people that do that.. hear all the nut vibrating loose in their MOTORCYCLES... and no, it doesn't matter if it is AMERICAN-MADE, JAPANESE-MADE, or anything else... be a little bit courteous to the people around you.. That is the bottom line. It seems that society has forgotten all about that."<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> he completely ignores it (knowing I've just made a point), whines about being called names and weakly attempts to insult my manhood because of my lack of a Harley in my garage.  Ummmm... yeah, whatever. <P>Hypocrite? Let's see... he claims stereo-pumpers aren't cool because they annoy other people (a point which I agree with), but seems to think that his Harley exhaust is the sounds of angels from Heaven to all who are fortunate enough to be within earshot.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Oh, and also for the record - you are wrong when you claim "at least one person here thinks so since I don't agree with him". I don't think that you're a hypocrite because we disagree with each other - use a dictionary if you have to to learn what 'hypocrite' *really* means, but it's not 'person who holds a differing opinion' -  I think you are a hypocrite because you berate others for annoying you with their noise, noise that they seem to think is enjoyable, while you proudly crow about making noise that you seem to think is enjoyable, in fact, it is just as much a nuisance as the noise you are complaining about. I personally am annoyed by both types of noise, so I agree with half of what you're saying. However, at least I am consistant with my views, when you are in fact, hypocritical with yours on the subject.<P>Thanks for making my point for me so very clearly. Have a great day.  <P>EDITED only to fix UBBCodes, and to add clarification to the 'you are wrong' statement.<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||09-02-2001||10:05 AM||||I'll explain myself yet again about that one... I don't run straight pipes.. just a little louder than stock, but as I have said repeatedly not much louder than a car and certainly not as loud as those stereos.<P>And the reason I ignored your paraphrasing of my statement is because you had already ignored the point of the paragraph above many times so your changed words actually don't apply to what we were talking about.<P>Thanks for the vote everyone. As has been pointed out, everyone has their opinions and I always fight for the right for those opinions. As Roger said, we often are on different sides of an issue but when it comes down to it was still respect each other. Actually, Roger is one of my favorite people here because I always look forward to his posts. I don't think we disagree as much as he thinks we do.<P>If you think I am a hypocrite or worse, I am sorry for that.. but you have that right. And just to say it one more time.... My Harley ain't loud!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||09-02-2001||10:17 AM||||A hippo crate? Ive heard of harleys being called 'crates' before, but I dont think Songman is hippo!<P>  Everyone knows that decreasing the backpressure on an internal combustion engine increases HP.<P>  Also there are noise cancellation mufflers available for cars that can make the exhaust completely silent! they have not been implemented for two reason:<P> 1. a silent car would be dangerous. Pedestrians are use to being able to hear a car coming, and they depend on that info subconsciously. If we start putting silent cars onthe streets then alot more pedistrains, and bicycle riders are gonna get hit.<P> 2. People expect their engines to go zroommm when they step onthe pedal, its a form of feedback, like when you are pulling out at a corner and you step onthe gas, you hear the car respond, or you hear nothing and know it has just stalled. <P> but the bottom line is putting lower pressure pipes on a motorcycle IS functinal -the bike runs better, and people hear you coming - both are important.<P>  blasting your car stereo at a red light does not improve anything for anyone<P> and BTW, even though Songman and I seem to bang elbows on the forum every once in a while, we have sent personal emails back and forth to clear the air - we dont agree on some things, but he's ok in my book.||||reg||10
Z||000012||spideyfoot||09-02-2001||10:32 AM||||I sleep during the day and the only thing that wakes me up seems to be lawn mowers. Thats it Im moving to Vegas.||||reg||1
