Z||000037||Formula88||09-02-2001||11:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>And Formula, you asked specifically if I ran straight pipes so this is not an attempt to keep anything going... No, I do not. I replaced my factory tips with slant cuts which are still mufflers and just slightly <BR>louder than factory...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Man, that makes all the difference in the world!  I was (and I think LZ was) referring to the ones with straight pipes.  We've got a lot of those running around here.  Actually, it's rare to see a Harley around here with any kind of muffler, unless it's a highway cruiser loaded with saddle bags, fairing and the whole 9...<P>That takes the hipocracy right out, IMO, cuz slightly louder than stock doesn't seem unreasonable.  Just as loud music (within certain limits) isn't unreasonalble. <P>Glad to see everyone came out of this only slightly crisp.  Time for beer!   <IMG SRC="http://www.ukobservers.net/cwm/otn/party/beerchug.gif">  ||||reg||14
