Z||000043||Boomtastic||09-03-2001||08:12 AM||||Sorry mate, I can't agree with you on the Harley issue (which set off the fire). Living down the street from one of the Hell's Angels bars, I hear them coming like gang busters, and that's okay?! Would I rather hear rice rocket bikes screaming up and down the street (since I own one)? No. Or loud stereos booming all the time (since I own one)? No. When was the last time you heard about a Harley rider getting pulled over for "noise"? What you hear - what has been come to be known as "the Harley sound" is NOT what comes from the factory. That obnoxious sound comes from modifying the exhaust illegally, yet it is okay. Well, to each his own. Does it bother me or hurt me in any way that their pipes are loud? Naw - in 3 seconds they've past my house and I could give a poop less. What DOES bother me is that people are trying to justify the noise, and that they are getting away with it since the law turns a blind eye. That burns me up. I've been stopped and cited for a loud stereo system. It was around 12:30 am, in a very rural (read "farm area") setting, and I had the windows down and the stereo up a little louder than the local police man desired. Was it really that loud? Probably not, but under the circumstances I must have been disturbing the night life (those crickets get all pissy when you wake them). The real problem comes when we pass laws that leave the judgement up to the individual officer. Making judgement calls is not the job of the officers. They are there to uphold laws, not interpert them as they see fit. There is no clear cut standards here for "noise pollution", and as such we have poor laws regarding it. Perhaps this is why the Harleys are allowed to run straight pipes, yet I cannot on my car. Interesting ...<P>Let's address the issue that "loud pipes save lives". Right. That's another BS story that can be likened to the "lights on for safety" crap you hear about from the "Big 3" car makers. When was the last time that daytime driving lights saved anyone? Motorcycles have been running daytime headlights for years, however to this day people have a hard time seeing them on the road. It's pure BS that daytime headlamps - or loud exhausts - save lives, *unless* you have your headlamps on during rain or other inclement weather, but then you are not using "daytime running lights", you're using common sense.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000044||Wolfhound||09-03-2001||08:34 AM||||One of the oldest excuses for killing someone on a bike is "I didn't see him". It's bull- It should translate to I pulled out in front of him because he didn't intimidate me the way pulling out in front of a semi would have. I though he would stop.||||reg||13
Z||000045||Songman||09-03-2001||11:45 AM||||This is all just for the record and meant to address the latest comments since we are all one big happy family again...<P>There is a lot of difference in a Harley with aftermarket pipes on it and a Hell's Angels biker bar... <P>And sometime when you are on the interstate and look in your mirrors and don't see anything, you'll hear that rumble of that Harley in your blind spot. You won't hear that Honda there. Personally, I never change lanes without looking over my shoulder. I don't trust mirrors. Lots of folks just use mirrors if even that much...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||6
Z||000046||84Bill||09-04-2001||08:22 AM||||Hey Songman if you want to be a doctor than more power to ya. Just stop sending me email telling me to wear a seatbelt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000047||Voytek||09-04-2001||12:22 PM||||Boomtastic - I couldn't have said it better myself.<P>There IS a double standard out there.  Most Harleys I hear (including the 2 in my neighborhood and the ones that pull up to me at a light) are waaaay friggin louder than some of the loudest stereos.  In fact, some of these bikes are so loud that I need ear plugs when they go by.  And what's worse, a lot of these idiots rev their engines on purpose, just to annoy everyone around.  Do they ever get pulled over for noise violations?  No.<P>Songman - to answer your original question, yes, I do believe you are a hypocrite on this particular topic.  I'm not knocking your bike 'cause I've never heard it.  Yes, there are way too many **** *y drivers out there and too many riders ran over but I don't agree that loud exhaust will save anyone's life.  That's what a horn is for!!!!<P>As for bikers with Harleys and loud exhausts, it's not the pipes that allow people to notice them in the blind spot - it's their wide rear ends and cheeks that hang on either side of the seat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> .  And maybe the fact that people are afraid of getting shot if they put a scratch on the fat man's bike.<P>Oh, and I have yet to hear a car stereo that's louder than a modified Harley's exhaust.  I'll take a loud stereo outside of my window at 5 AM over a Harley engine any day.<P>Daytime running lights?  There is another BS idea that I don't even want to get into.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000048||Songman||09-04-2001||01:11 PM||||I am having such a hard time making people understand that I am not talking straight pipes! I am talking slant cut muffler tips! <P>And to be totally fair.. if you go back to the original post, I am not the one who brought Harleys into it, nor am I the one who said Loud Pipes Saves Lives. I just became the brunt of everyone argument.<P>Do I think loud pipes save lives? Yes, I do.. But I never mentioned anything about exceedingly loud pipes either. This was all brought up by people who wanted to call me a hypocrite. I have said over and over since the start that my f#$*&^* Harley is NOT LOUD!<P>And wide asses? I think you need to quit watching so many 60s Hell's Angels movies. Personally, I am 6'2", 210 pounds. Don't see how that can qualify for a wide ass.<P>For those who apparently can't read MY HARLEY IS NOT LOUD any of the 100 times I have typed it before, I think you are just looking for a reason to jump on a bandwagon that has already gone. The reason for this thread has already been settled. It is now just looking like people skipping what they don't want to read just to try to start a problem back up...<P>One more time for the people in the cheap seats who missed it before...<BR><B>I AM NOT THE ONE WHO STARTED THE HARLEY CONVERSATION!<P>I DO NOT HAVE STRAIGHT PIPES! MY HARLEY IS NOT LOUD!<P>I NEVER EVER SAID THAT THOSE UNGODLY LOUD HARLEYS WERE NOT ANNOYING!<P>AND FOR AS MUCH AS SOME OF YOU ARE DYING TO SAY IT, FOR THE REASONS ABOVE, I AM NOT A HYPOCRITE ON THIS SUBJECT.</B><P>But at least you all did do one thing.. you took the attention off of what everyone was really talking about... LOUD ASS STEREOS.<p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||8
