Z||000051||84Bill||09-04-2001||01:33 PM||||You use slant cut mufflers? heh, gloves are alot cheaper and much more fasionable   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BTW Black gloves are definatly not as loud as a red muffler even a brown muffler is not as loud. Fluressent colors are a definate 10 on the loud-o-meter. Just hope this helps clear the air  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000052||Voytek||09-04-2001||02:36 PM||||Since I know that some (or all?) of your last post, Songman, is directed as a reply to me, please note:  NEITHER I, NOR ANYONE HERE IS KNOCKING YOUR BIKE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>As I SAID IN MY POST, 'I've never heard your bike'.<P>Now that we got that out of the way, let me clarify one more thing.  READ MY POSTS CORRECTLY!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>(Isn't that what you were asking for?)<BR>I didn't comment on YOUR a$$ (I've never seen it, and have no desire to  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  Why you're telling me (or everyone) your height/weight ... beats me.  FYI: I'm 6'-1" and about 190 lbs.  Oh, and I think my a$$ is just the right size, too.<P><BR>As far as being a hypocrite?  Well, you asked for opinions, did you not?  So now it's OK for everyone to kiss your rear but not OK to vote 'yes'?  Let me explain why I do think you're a hipocrite on THIS topic:<BR>Did you not say in the other thread 'I shouldn't have to listen to someone else's music at a red light' .... 'be a little curteous to people around you..'?  Or, 'loud stereos are for open road.'  Well, guess what, I don't see the 2 bikers in my neighborhood installing a muffler prior to riding by my house.<P>In fact, you mention courtesy more than once.  Have you ever considered that a deafening biker next to my car is not courteous?  Well, that IMHO makes you a hypocrite.<P>You asked for opinions, now don't get peeved off when you get them.  I came here to reply to your own question, not to start a war (unless, of course, this was intended as 'Praise The Songman' thread - then I misunderstood and I'm sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ).<P>Oh, and don't be so sensitive.  No one was attacking your own Harley - YOU're the one who brough up your bike in the other thread.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
