Z||000056||Pontiaddict||09-04-2001||11:40 PM||||My friends dad had a 900 Kawasaki that he runs, for the most part, with a gutted aftermarket muffler, if he needs to, before he leaves the house, he can put the diffuser abck into it. But that isn't my point.<BR>My point is, sitting at my friends house, you can hear the bike on the highway (obvious who's it is by the sound) almost 5 minutes before he gets it home. Yet, if he comes home late, he' goes through town quietly enough not to draw attention to himself. Granted, it's still comparatively loud, but it's not window shaking, eardrum piercing loud like it's capable of being.<BR>The bikers that leave at closing time, on the other hand, will rev the crap out of their bikes before tearing through town, liquored up and not caring about anyone.<BR>Who do you think I would rather hear at 2 in the morning?||||reg||1
